/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Reference Miro exports of a real board — a `.rtb` backup, an SVG oracle, a PDF and
# a CSV. Hundreds of megabytes of someone's real work; kept locally as the import
# oracle (see docs/02-miro-formats.md) and never committed.
#
# Anchored to the repo root so they only catch the exports sitting there — an
# unanchored `*.svg` would also swallow assets/logo/. Exports whose filename has no
# extension are not matched by these; put a pattern for those in `.git/info/exclude`,
# which is local to your clone and never pushed.
/*.rtb
/*.svg
/*.pdf
/*.csv

# Real board content captured from the clipboard for analysis.
/captures

# Reference screenshots of a real Miro account, kept locally as the UI reference
# (see docs/04-ui-reference.md). They contain real board names.
/Screenshots

# The private working log. See RULES.md for the parts a contributor needs.
/CLAUDE.md

# The agent workspace: the project docs, the lessons, the skills and the agents.
# The docs and the lessons carry the same private content CLAUDE.md does.
/.claude/

# macOS folder metadata.
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode, from scripts/ and build.py.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The built browser bundle and any board snapshot exported for it. Both are generated by
# `cargo build --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --profile web -p vellum-web` plus
# `wasm-bindgen`, and a board snapshot is real board content, which never belongs in a
# public repository.
web/dist/
